      "role": "user",
      "sender": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Found 3 recently archived items across all workspaces (all archived 2026-10-18):\n\n1. **Birch itinerary conversation** \u2014 archived 2026-10-18 17:29 UTC\n   - Workspace: **Vault Trips** (also archived at the same time)\n   - Restorable as: chat only, or chat + workspace\n\n2. **Linden planning conversation** \u2014 the chat itself is *not* archived, but it lives in workspace **Atlas Research**, which was archived 2026-10-18 17:29 UTC\n   - Restorable as: workspace only\n\n3. **Maple archival notes** \u2014 archived 2026-10-18 17:29 UTC\n   - No workspace (standalone chat)\n   - Restorable as: chat only\n\nNo pagination \u2014 this is the complete set. Want me to request a restore for any of these?",
      "conversation_id": "864ea7cc-b854-48aa-910e-967209cfbd6d",
      "id": "8f620910-bfad-4a1c-9ce8-d64bbdce1fe3",
      "parent_message_id": "2b8bab96-8136-40a9-bc87-3bf62910a631",
      "role": "assistant",
      "sender": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "**Accomplished:** Located the 3 recently archived items (all 2026-10-18 17:29 UTC) and identified the second one: the **Linden planning conversation**, whose chat isn't archived but whose workspace **Atlas Research** is \u2014 restorable as *workspace only*.\n\n**Unfinished:** The restore was never issued. I couldn't retrieve the original `result_ref` (the earlier run's log isn't reachable under the current root), and the budget ran out before I could re-search.\n\n**To finish:** Re-run the archived-search, take the `result_ref` for the Atlas Research item, and call `request_conversation_restore` with workspace-only scope.",
